# Functions `go tool deadcode` reports as unreachable from cmd/localcode
# that are known and accepted. One name per line; a "#" comment says why.
#
# scripts/check-deadcode.sh fails on anything reported that is not here,
# and on anything here that is no longer reported. The second direction
# matters as much as the first: an allowlist nobody has to maintain
# becomes a list of names that used to mean something.
#
# What this file is NOT is a verdict that these are fine. Five of them are
# genuinely uncalled and are candidates for removal; they are listed
# rather than deleted because deleting them is a change to the product
# and this commit is a change to the gate. See the notes below.

# --- reachable only from tests -------------------------------------
# deadcode runs with -test=false, so a function whose only callers are
# tests is reported. That is the right setting: -test=true would call
# every exported function reachable and report almost nothing.
internal/agent/compact.go:compactSystemBlocks
internal/agent/context_budget.go:contextWindow
internal/commands/commands.go:Expand
internal/memory/memory.go:SystemPromptSection
internal/smart/smart.go:Builtins

# --- test hooks, called from production code by a test that sets them --
# Both are set by a test and read by the code under test, so no static
# call site exists in either direction.
internal/agent/fallback.go:setRetryWaitBarrier
internal/agent/schedule.go:unattendedWaitForTest

# --- build-tag variant ------------------------------------------------
# The non-Windows no-op half of a pair. The Windows file's HideConsole has
# the caller (internal/dialog/reveal_windows.go); this one is compiled on
# every other platform and called by nobody there, which is what "does
# nothing outside Windows" means.
internal/childproc/childproc_other.go:HideConsole

# --- genuinely uncalled, pending a decision ---------------------------
# No caller anywhere in this tree, tests included. Left in place rather
# than removed because removal is its own change and one of them is not
# as dead as it looks: turnTracker.anyRunning has a live caller on the
# branch in .claude/worktrees/bold-golick-d93a50 (workspace.go), so
# deleting it here would break that work on merge. The turnTracker three
# sit in the turn-admission tracker that v0.55.0 rewrote four times.
# memory.SystemPromptSection above is the same shape one step further
# along: it lost its production caller in the v0.57.0 trust split and
# still has tests describing it as "used at daemon startup".
internal/agent/loop.go:Loop.systemPromptFor
internal/agent/rehydrate.go:dataStrings
internal/daemon/turns.go:turnTracker.busy
internal/daemon/turns.go:turnTracker.anyRunning
internal/daemon/turns.go:turnTracker.whileIdle
